<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Pacific Dunlop appoints new director.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Pacific Dunlop appoints new director.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian industrial conglomerate Pacific Dunlop Ltd said on Monday it had appointed former Tubemakers chief executive Tony Daniels as a director.</p>
<p>Daniels retired as Tubemakers of Australia managing director in 1995. The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd bought out Tubemakers in 1996.</p>
<p>Pacific Dunlop chairman John Gough said in a statement that Daniels would bring to the board extensive experience in international business and manufacturing.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
